-- title:
--   Sections avoiding the origin span the formal chart
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative local ring, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $T$, and $P$ a section of the projective Weierstrass model of $W$, i.e. a morphism $P_1 \colon \operatorname{Spec} T \to \mathrm{Proj}$-model of $W$ together with the identity $P_1$ followed by the structure morphism $= \mathrm{id}_{\operatorname{Spec} T}$. Write `OriginChartRing W` for the degree-zero homogeneous localisation of the graded quotient ring of the model away from the coordinate $Y$ (`coord W 1`), with its elements $xOverY$ and $zOverY$ given by $X/Y$ and $Z/Y$. Assume: (i) for every ring homomorphism $\chi \colon$ `OriginChartRing W` $\to T$ the predicate `ReducesToOrigin P χ (maximalIdeal T)` fails, that is, it is never the case that `IsOriginChartSection P χ` holds and both `originParam χ` and `originW χ` lie in the maximal ideal of $T$; (ii) $\Phi \colon$ `OriginChartRing W` $\to T[\![X]\!]$ is a ring homomorphism which sends the image of $t \in T$ under the canonical map from the degree-zero piece to the constant series $C(t)$, sends $xOverY$ to $-X$, and sends $zOverY$ to $-w_W$, where $w_W$ is the power series $\sum_n \mathrm{coeff}_n(W.wIter\,n)X^n$ of the formal group of $W$. Then the ideal of $T[\![X]\!]$ generated by the image, under the global-sections identification $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec}$ `OriginChartRing W`$) \cong$ `OriginChartRing W` followed by $\Phi$, of the ideal cut out on the whole of $\operatorname{Spec}$ `OriginChartRing W` by the pullback along the origin-chart open immersion `originChartι W` of the kernel ideal sheaf of $P_1$, is the unit ideal.
--
--   This is the "missing the origin" dichotomy at the level of the formal chart: a section whose reduction does not pass through the origin contributes a unit, hence no divisor, to the formal parameter. It is used in the analysis of divisors of Drinfeld bases, namely in [`WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.IsDrinfeldBasis.exists_isUnit_mul_nthSeries_eq_prod_X_sub_C_originParam`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.IsDrinfeldBasis.exists_isUnit_mul_nthSeries_eq_prod_X_sub_C_originParam) and in [`WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.torsionIdeal_le_basisDivisor_of_nsmul_eq_one_of_nthSeries_eq_mul_prod`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.torsionIdeal_le_basisDivisor_of_nsmul_eq_one_of_nthSeries_eq_mul_prod).
